  "model": "TCP46 and TCP46A",
  "models": [
    "TCP46",
    "TCP46-24",
    "TCP46A"
  ],
  "vendor_website": "tecnolog.ind.br",
  "description": "Programmable controller with 18 digital inputs, 16 relay outputs, analog inputs and outputs, Ethernet and RS485 Modbus RTU: hardware I/O, clock and holiday registers",
  "revision": 1,
  "revised": "2026-11-18",
  "source": "Tecnolog, manual of the TCP line of controllers (Portuguese), section 8.1",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Manual dos CLPs Tecnolog linha TCP - TCP46, TCP46-24, TCP46EX, TCP46A, TCP-IoT e TCP17",
      "url": "https://downloads.tecnolog.ind.br/downloads/CLPs/Tecnolog/Manual%20dos%20CLPs%20Tecnolog%20linha%20TCP%20%20-%20TCP46%2C%20TCP46-24%2C%20TCP46EX%2CTCP46A%2C%20TCP-IoT%20e%20TCP17.pdf",
      "note": "chapter 8, Modbus address tables, and the Modbus slave blocks of chapters 7 and 9",
      "accessed": "2026-11-18",
      "sha256": "46c32bf1703f06ea066caea03f0101d7ad34874cf36679fe4cfa5d36f3343f14"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "TCP46 and TCP46A with the TCP46EX expansion (up to 8 modules). The manual marks some addresses as TCP46A only (in red) and the analog inputs 20100 to 20153 as present on both, with the temperature reading limited to the TCP46A; the red marks do not survive in the text of the PDF, so the model split is not recorded here.",
    "The status registers do not agree in meaning in the manual: NTC_01 to NTC_08 say 1 is normal and 0 a fault, the others (NTC_09 to NTC_18, AI_1 to AI_8) say 0 is valid.",
    "The holiday list holds 20 holidays as day and month pairs from 20650; the daylight saving registers hold the start day and month and the end day and month.",
    "Programmable controller: the tables below are the fixed hardware map. Any other data (set points, counters, results of the logic) is exposed by MDBS blocks in the user program made with TProg, at the registers chosen there; those are not listed. Writes outside the limits set in an MDBS block are ignored.",
    "Floating-point values take two registers with the high word first (ABCD); 16-bit values keep AB. The address is sent as written, with no offset (20000 is protocol address 20000).",
    "The Modbus RTU slave (RS485) and Modbus TCP/UDP (Ethernet, port 502) are enabled and configured in the web server of the controller (speed, parity, stop bits, address, transmission delay); the manual gives no factory values for the serial port. Functions 01 to 06 and 16 are supported by the master side; the manual does not list the slave functions.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "unit_id": 1,
